the trade control and expert system  known as traces is an online management  tool of the European Commission that  tracks the movements of animals food  feed and plants imported from outside  the EU or traveling through the  countries of the European Union each  year vast quantities of livestock and  produce are traded into the European  Union to be served on 500 million  European plates raising the question how  can the European Commission ensure that  both food and consumers are kept safe  the European Commission requires  consignments to be accompanied by health  certificates or trade documents and  national authorities may post these  documents online through traces in  addition border control authorities must  check all of the certificates to allow a  consignment to enter and travel through  each European Member State when animals  and animal products vegetables and  plants even wood and organic products  and feed and food of non animal origin  as well are exported to the European  Union  Tracie's manages the official controls  and route planning quickly and  efficiently online  the system manages and monus's thousands  of documents which significantly reduces  the administrative burden on economic  operators and governmental authorities  in simple terms the moment of economic  operator decides to export a consignment  of goods it enters the necessary data  into the Tracie's system more than  25,000 users worldwide connect to traces  to track consignments in 33 languages 24  hours a day seven days a week  generating 1 million emails per day and  more than 1 million certificates per  year and each year online traces manages  500,000 intra-union trade certificates  and 500,000 border control documents so  when a consignment is declared at a  European Union border everyone concerned  from economic operator to control  Authority can check the certificates  through the same information system  greatly simplifying and accelerating the  entire trading process  during transportation the journey each  can sign man takes is carefully  specified and monitored and like  individual footprints this tracking  creates traceability so should there be  a problem with an animal or product the  system quickly tracks back to the  original source of the problem and  forward to the destination by tracking  importation flows precisely however  complex a route might be traces can  respond quickly to problems providing  both consumers and livestock with  greater security and protection plus by  quickly detecting abnormalities in data  the system helps prevent fraudulent  trading in fact 70 countries now  participate in traces 28 European Union  38 non European Union and for EFTA  countries to facilitate exports to and  through Europe in short traces  encourages cooperation and facilitates  trading from farm to fork  and using traces will become even more  quick and easy in the near future by  2015 traces aims to stop using paper  everything will be available digitally  even signatures and you'll be able to  operate the system on tablets and mobile  phones too  traces is a major leap forward in  tracking the movements of livestock and  produce monitoring animal diseases and  combating fraud whilst significantly  speeding up administrative procedures  traces protecting consumers facilitating  trade  Oh
 

